<div class="wrap">
  <div class="card">
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <h3>What do the Gold and Silver badges mean?</h3>
    <p><span class="tag gold">Gold</span> means fully made or grown in the UK, including the main material. <span class="tag silver">Silver</span> means genuinely made in the UK but with an imported main material or some imported stock. Products merely designed, branded, printed or packed in the UK don&rsquo;t qualify at all.</p>
    <h3>Why is a famous British brand only Silver?</h3>
    <p>Because the tier follows the material, not the reputation. Northampton&rsquo;s great shoemakers are Silver because the calf leather is imported &mdash; superb British making, imported main material. The badge is a statement of fact, not a criticism.</p>
    <h3>Do businesses pay to be listed?</h3>
    <p>No. Nobody pays for a listing, a badge, or placement &mdash; and nobody can. Tiers are decided by evidence alone, and every listing shows its evidence publicly.</p>
    <h3>How do businesses get on the map?</h3>
    <p>We research and verify each listing against public evidence &mdash; the business&rsquo;s own website, its stated materials and making locations. Anyone can <a href="submit.html">suggest a business</a>; every suggestion is checked against the standard before it appears.</p>
    <h3>Something on the map is wrong &mdash; how do I report it?</h3>
    <p>Please <a href="contact.html">contact us</a> with the listing name and what&rsquo;s wrong. If a business believes its tier understates it &mdash; for example, we couldn&rsquo;t evidence where its clay or fabric comes from &mdash; we&rsquo;ll gladly review with better evidence.</p>
    <h3>Why are Northern Ireland and the Isle of Man included?</h3>
    <p>Northern Ireland is part of the UK. The Isle of Man is a Crown dependency rather than part of the UK &mdash; we include it under a broader British Isles view, and we say so openly (it&rsquo;s home to some of the finest making in these islands).</p>
    <h3>Why isn&rsquo;t my favourite maker listed?</h3>
    <p>Probably because we haven&rsquo;t got to them yet &mdash; the map grows in researched batches. <a href="submit.html">Tell us about them</a> and we&rsquo;ll check them out.</p>
    <h3>Is this sponsored or affiliated with anyone?</h3>
    <p>No. Buy British is independent, carries no advertising, takes no commission, and has no connection to any retailer or trade body.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<script>
const burgerBtn = document.getElementById('burger'), burgerMenu = document.getElementById('menu');
burgerBtn.addEventListener('click', e => {
  e.stopPropagation();
  const open = !burgerMenu.hasAttribute('hidden');
  if (open) { burgerMenu.setAttribute('hidden',''); } else { burgerMenu.removeAttribute('hidden'); }
  burgerBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!open));
});
document.addEventListener('click', e => {
  if (!burgerMenu.hasAttribute('hidden') && !burgerMenu.contains(e.target)) burgerMenu.setAttribute('hidden','');
});
</script>
